HTTPS diagnostic overlay19 — prepared, not executed

The overlay is derived from frozen candidate-snapshot-18 (2,282 files). It adds one diagnostic helper and instruments only JPIPHTTPSRequest.swift, JPIPTransport.swift and CodexR3HTTPStreamingTests.swift, producing a 2,283-file derived manifest. No main repository file, frozen source, historical overlay or prior receipt was edited. No compiler, native test, codec, server, Git or network action was performed. Independent review is required before root-owned execution. Never merge this tracer or use an instrumented pass as an uninstrumented gate.

The four selected cases are the failed ordinary17 tests: absoluteDeadlineCancelsSilentResponse, sharedHTTPSPathPreservesRequestHeadersBodyAndNegotiatedChannel, completionAndCancellationHaveOneWinner (both existing arguments), and completedRequestEventuallyReleasesItsDelegateOwnership. Each has an entry stamp and exit flush; the parameterised test permits two exits, so five selected-test flushes are possible. Shared request/delegate/URLProtocol instrumentation also records other HTTPS requests. No test selection, declaration, argument, assertion, concurrency setting, timeout, absolute clock origin, queue priority or queue suspension policy changes. Current userInitiated delegate QoS and exact oversize-admission assertions come from frozen18, not historical11.

