  python3 -B work/https-diagnostic-19/static_check.py

Root may copy overlay/ over a separate copy of frozen18 and verify every file against diagnostic-source-manifest.json. Do not copy these files into the main checkout. The generator follows historical11's exact asserted replacement pattern, but reads frozen18 and the new bounded trace-helper.swift. The full delta against18 is overlay-delta.patch. Static checks verify current/main traced-input hashes, deadline/queue/suspension expressions, all test declarations and expectation expressions, and whitespace. They are not a Swift compiler or semantic proof.

Every emitted event contains DispatchTime uptime nanoseconds, an owner UUID (or named caller), hostname and phase. Owner-host binding links request owners, test callers, scenario owners and URLProtocol owners without retaining requests or response Data. Test entry, request read entry and caller wake record Task.currentPriority.rawValue. Delegate queue creation records its configured qualityOfService and serial count. These are observed properties, not proof of effective execution priority or scheduling guarantees.

Phase coverage:
- Caller marks immediately precede forming/passing the unchanged deadlines; post-await or caught-error marks identify caller resumption. The silent case retains the original start instant and120ms deadline; its caught-error marker precedes the unchanged two-second elapsed assertion. Logging inside this measured interval is an acknowledged perturbation.
- HTTPS transport send entry/preflight, URL-timeout preflight, owner creation, registration observer, before/after read, publication observer, final deadline recheck and deadline error remapping are distinct. A preflight that fails before owner creation has host-correlated transport marks.
- Request read entry/remaining interval, single-use claim, watchdog preflight/error/scheduled, continuation/start, session/task creation and publication, hooks and resume are stamped. Watchdog firing and task cancellation are separate. Result-get error, cancellation check, final deadline check and read exit distinguish a generic preflight error from stored callback error or a final caller recheck.
- Delegate response/body-first/admission error, task completion, finishTasksAndInvalidate, invalidation, serial-tail enqueue/execution, completion publication, continuation resume and caller wake expose the relevant intervals. Scripted callback tests still inject their same callbacks inside their unchanged publication hook; these are not additional real network callbacks.
- URLProtocol startLoading entry versus serial-block entry, scenario begin, response submission/return, chunks1/2/100, finish submission/return and stopLoading entry/block entry separate harness scheduling from Foundation/delegate delivery. Protocol modes and random hostnames are correlated. The silent protocol deliberately submits no response.
- Request deinit and the existing deinit observer are recorded without adding a request-retaining edge. A tail captures the standalone trace object, not its JPIPHTTPSRequest owner.

Bounded capture and limitations:
The registry retains at most128 trace stores, each with at most128 events between flushes, plus one128-event caller correlation store. Owner/host text is capped at128 characters and event text at1,024 characters; line breaks are escaped. A first-event set is capped at eight keys. Capacity losses are counted and reported as droppedEvents/droppedOwners. Store registration and each store use Mutex. Trace locks never call back into request locks. No printing, file writing, timer, queue canary or new work queue is added to callbacks/watchdogs.

Only selected test-exit defers flush. They copy buffered events and print synchronously under a separate output mutex. Output formatting, allocation, locks, timestamp reads and printing can affect scheduling of other concurrent work; no zero-overhead claim is made. Flush groups and registry traversal are not chronological: analyse original timestamps. A callback/deinit event after the last flush is censored, not evidence that it never occurred. Truncation, capacity loss or process failure also prevents a completeness claim. The tracer neither joins callbacks nor adds a final process-wide flush. If a selected caller never returns, its own exit flush may be absent.

Interpretation must stay source-scoped and diagnostic. Large preflight/await/callback intervals localise delay but do not identify the scheduler's sole cause. Failed ordinary17 receipts remain failed, and no later diagnostic pass qualifies source18. The four failures and their timing were retained in candidate-full-17/native.log. No acceptance, platform qualification, external-peer result or gate waiver follows from preparation.

All overlay and receipt writes are stopped.
